SUMMARY:Exhibition: "Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and Hallucinations"
LOCATION:Worth Ryder Art Gallery\, Anthropology &amp\; Art Building\, Rm 1
 16
DESCRIPTION:The Department of German and the Department of Art Practice ar
 e excited to announce the opening of Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and
  Hallucinations\, curated by Antonio Somaini with Hannes Bajohr\, Sonja Th
 iel and Elena Yu\, in dialogue with the France&#8211\;Berkeley research in
 itiative The Latent Spaces of Culture\, and on display at the Worth Ryder 
 Art Gallery.In neural networks\, the "hidden layers" are the intermediate 
 strata of transformation between input and output — the computational st
 ructures where data are transformed\, weighted\, and recombined into incre
 asingly abstract\, distributed representations that no human eye can read.
  The exhibition Hidden Layers: AI Infrastructures and Hallucinations takes
  this term as its conceptual frame\, bringing together seventeen internati
 onal artists and researchers working at the intersection of contemporary a
 rt and machine learning to make visible what artificial intelligence keeps
  out of sight: its planetary infrastructures and computational latent spac
 es\, its colonial and ideological underpinnings\, its misrecognitions and 
 hallucinations\, and its transformation of our relation to the past throug
 h the silent reprocessing of pre-existing cultural forms. The exhibition i
 s organized in four sections: "In the Latent Spaces of Culture\," "Materia
 l Infrastructures\," "Colonial Imaginaries: From Misrecognition to Generat
 ive Slopaganda\," and "Hallucinations and Psychedelia."Featuring works by 
 Nouf Aljowaysir (https://www.noufaljowaysir.com/)\; Gašper and Nina Begu
 š & Metahaven (https://latentspacecraft.antikythera.org/)\; Grégory Chat
 onsky (https://chatonsky.net/)\; Kate Crawford & Vladan Joler (https://ana
 tomyof.ai/)\; Asma Kazmi (https://www.asmakazmi.com/) & Jill Miller (https
 ://www.jillmiller.net/)\; Andrea Khôra (https://www.andreakhora.com/)\; O
 ccitane Lacurie & Barnabé Sauvage (https://www.schirn.de/en/schirnmag/3-q
 uestions-for-occitane-lacurie-und-barnabe-sauvage/)\; Greg Niemeyer (https
 ://www.gregniemeyer.com/)\; and Mario Santamaria (https://mariosantamaria.
 net/) & Alex Saum-Pascual (https://www.alexsaum.com/).Hidden Layers is a c
 ollaboration between the Department of German and the Worth Ryder Art Gall
 ery at the Department of Art Practice. It is part of the France–Berkeley
  research initiative The Latent Spaces of Culture: a collaboration between
  UC Berkeley\, the Université Sorbonne Nouvelle in Paris\, and the French
  National Center for Scientific Research (CNRS).Exhibition Dates: Septembe
 r 3 - October 3\, 2026Opening Reception: Thursday\, September 3\, 4-6:30pm
 \, Worth Ryder Art Gallery RSVP (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 Sd_OOMe7YQHw3CYbSr673UCSlQ0f4mn4lZ7g46KhRUTRpC5qQ/viewform)Artist Talk\, G
 regory Chatonsky "INFRALLUCINATION": Thursday\, September 3\, 6:30-8:00pm\
 , AAPB 285 RSVP (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd_OOMe7YQHw3CYb
 Sr673UCSlQ0f4mn4lZ7g46KhRUTRpC5qQ/viewform)Film Program\, Push Buttons and
  AI (https://bampfa.org/event/push-buttons-and-ai): September 9\, 7 pm\, B
 AMPFA RSVP (https://bampfa.org/event/push-buttons-and-ai)Curatorial Tour\,
  led by Antonio Somaini: Friday\, September 11\, 4:30pm\, Worth Ryder Art 
 Gallery Workshop on Latent Space of Culture: September 9\, 2pm-4pm\; Septe
 mber 10/11\, 9:30 am-4pm on both days\, 470 StephensBerkeley AI Futures Sa
 lon (https://bids.berkeley.edu/berkeley-ai-futures-salon): On the Subject 
 of Art in Artificial Intelligence: September 16\, 6:30pm– 9pm Apply to a
 ttend (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSenC1GtID5I8JrILQqwW3cL4sF
 hgbc3BagB6aoh10Q1WK8aQA/viewform)Tour of AI: October 3 Reservations requir
 ed. Information forthcomingClosing day: October 3\, 12-3pm\, Worth Ryder A
 rt Gallery Open to the public\, no RSVP required&#160\;Additional events\,
  details\, and registration links to be announced. Times subject to change
 \, please also check the campus calendar (https://events.berkeley.edu/art)
 .This exhibition is supported by the France-Berkeley Fund of the Institute
  of European Studies\, the Department of German and the Department of Art 
 Practice\, together with the Berkeley Center for New Media\, the Berkeley 
 Institute for Data Science (BIDS)\, Department of Rhetoric\; Antikythera\,
  the Human Technology Futures (HTF)\, the Pamela P. Fong and Family Distin
 guished Chair in China Studies\, the Division of Arts & Humanities\, the T
 ownsend Center for the Humanities and the School of Information\, the Tech
 nology Network of the Berkeley Economy and Society Initiative (BESI)\, and
  the Berkeley Art\, Law\, and Finance Project\, hosted by the Berkeley Cen
 ter for Law and Business at Berkeley Law.&#160\;In conjunction with the ex
 hibition\, additional programming is developed in collaboration with Berke
 ley Art Museum and Pacific Film Archive (BAMPFA) and the Institute for Con
 temporary Art San Jose.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/324408-exhibition-hi
 dden-layers-ai-infrastructures-and-hallu
END:VEVENT
